zM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTIwMDM4/NS0xNjAzNDk2NTQ1/LTYxNDIuanBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/p5z7OSB9cDNMZvjhQsf-skQHOoc2JWRAHwIbUAyb6Oc/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTIwMDM4/NS0xNjAzNDk2NTQ1/LTYxNDIuanBlZw.jpeg","profile":"Hip-Hop label and retail store based in Houston, Texas.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:200385","relations":{"parentLabel":null,"sublabels":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/200385-SoSouth","type":"label","urls":["http://www.sosouth.com","https://www.facebook.com/SoSouthDigital","https://www.twitter.com/SoSouth","https://www.instagram.com/sosouthtx","https://www.myspace.com/sosouthcom"]}},"/api/discogs/label/281/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"281","image":"https://i.discogs.com/3HpIGTTfcLBKDF0WKsdSygbdfgirR7shFM3kGhgArBI/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:598/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTI4MS0x/NTAyNjQwNjY3LTQ4/MzMucG5n.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/VDDpno07NHdP4FibsyV_BYKKuBpw1B6aAXLmSNP8dQw/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTI4MS0x/NTAyNjQwNjY3LTQ4/MzMucG5n.jpeg","profile":"Blue Note is a label that is mostly known for its releases in the jazz genre.\r\n\r\nLabel Code: LC 0133 / LC 00133\r\n\r\nFounded by [a=Alfred Lion] and [a=Max Margulis] in 1939, the label was soon joined by Lion's childhood friend [a=Francis Wolff] (who took photographs during rehearsals used on LP sleeves). The early years saw BN issue 78rpm sides featuring traditional jazz artists and small-group swing, but from 1947 the company began to record the emerging bop movement with sides from [a=Thelonious Monk] and, in the next few years, [a=Bud Powell] and [a=Fats Navarro]. From the 1950s, Blue Note recorded musicians such as the Hammond organist [a=Jimmy Smith] and artists in the hard-bop idiom such as [a=Art Blakey & The Jazz Messengers]. Albums by long-time artists [a=Lee Morgan] (The Sidewinder)  and [a=Horace Silver] (Song For My Father) made a significant impact in the 1960s. Meanwhile, the label recorded more exploratory albums by  [a=Ornette Coleman] and [a=Cecil Taylor], among others\r\n\r\nLion sold the label to [l13531] in 1965 and retired in 1967. Wolff died in 1971. By now, more commercially-oriented music, including jazz-fusion, had started to be issued on the label, but in 1975, then-owners [l4898] launched a reissue program of Blue Note's back catalog which lasted until 1980. The previous year, Blue Note became a label of [l654].\r\n\r\nBeginning in 1982, Blue Note sessions began appearing in box-sets from [l100901] (co-owned by [a=Michael Cuscuna]). The label itself was relaunched as part of Capitol  subsidiary [l85486] in 1985 and began making new recordings, re-releasing albums and previously unissued material from the Lion-Wolff era found by Cuscuna.\r\n\r\nIn 1989, [l85486] was discontinued and Blue Note became the division under which all of Capitol-EMI's jazz activities were organized (two years later, [l85486] was revived for smooth jazz and pop-jazz releases). \r\n\r\nA 2005 reorganization at both [l654] and parent company [l26126] put Blue Note along with sister labels [l85486], Angel, Virgin Classics and Metro Blue under the Blue Note Label Group umbrella covering jazz, classical and adult pop recordings.\r\n\r\nIn 2012, [a62920] succeeded [a1120514] as Blue Note's president, and the label's owner, [l26126], was purchased by the [l38404].\r\n\r\nPlease note, many Blue Note issues also carry an [l26126] logo. This is not a label and [l=EMI] should not be added as a label. Instead it indicates that Blue Note was part of the EMI Group.\r\n\r\nBlue Note® is a registered trademark of [l87317]","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:281","relations":{"parentLabel":{"id":126439,"name":"Capitol Music Group"},"sublabels":[{"id":2163361,"name":"... E Ora Balliamo Con Il Jazz!"},{"id":596232,"name":"\"Unissued Masters\" Series"},{"id":283350,"name":"24 Bit By RVG"},{"id":3343782,"name":"313 Series"},{"id":562963,"name":"50th Anniversary Collection"},{"id":2106115,"name":"Audi Lounge by Blue Note"},{"id":676553,"name":"Back To Blue"},{"id":2408152,"name":"Ballads"},{"id":731171,"name":"Blue Brazil"},{"id":513790,"name":"Blue Break Beats"},{"id":448415,"name":"Blue Breakbeats"},{"id":1417667,"name":"Blue Instrumentalists"},{"id":501587,"name":"Blue Juice (2)"},{"id":784688,"name":"Blue Notables"},{"id":3779052,"name":"Blue Note 25 Best Albums"},{"id":664063,"name":"Blue Note 4000 Series Original Collection 100"},{"id":1637572,"name":"Blue Note 80 Vinyl Reissue Series"},{"id":3765085,"name":"Blue Note 85"},{"id":760013,"name":"Blue Note Best & More 1100"},{"id":419992,"name":"Blue Note BLP 1500 Series"},{"id":66004,"name":"Blue Note CLASSIC"},{"id":1945689,"name":"Blue Note Classic Vinyl Series"},{"id":1453652,"name":"Blue Note Classics"},{"id":284360,"name":"Blue Note Collector's Choice"},{"id":250978,"name":"Blue Note Connoisseur Series"},{"id":1261927,"name":"Blue Note Cover Series"},{"id":4636662,"name":"Blue Note Essential Vinyl Series"},{"id":123110,"name":"Blue Note International"},{"id":314283,"name":"Blue Note Jazz Classic Series"},{"id":1025295,"name":"Blue Note Legends"},{"id":969517,"name":"Blue Note Magazine"},{"id":464021,"name":"Blue Note Masterpiece (Vol.1)"},{"id":490333,"name":"Blue Note Masterpiece (Vol.2)"},{"id":464042,"name":"Blue Note Masterpiece (Vol.3)"},{"id":472179,"name":"Blue Note Masterpiece Selection 150"},{"id":794003,"name":"Blue Note Original 5000 Series Collection"},{"id":935328,"name":"Blue Note Plays"},{"id":275785,"name":"Blue Note Rare Groove Series"},{"id":681822,"name":"Blue Note Records 75th Anniversary Vinyl Initiative"},{"id":1380721,"name":"Blue Note Review"},{"id":663679,"name":"Blue Note The 4000 Series Collection"},{"id":1593136,"name":"Blue Note Tone Poet Series"},{"id":2563906,"name":"Blue Note Top Ten Series"},{"id":296589,"name":"Blue Note Trip"},{"id"